#Benifits of using MONGODB Database
MongoDb provides several advantages that make it a popular choice for modern application
SQL is like a strict paper form.

Everyone gets the exact same form with fields like Name, Age, and Address.

If you want to write down someone’s favorite food, you have to reprint the form for everyone with a new line for "Favorite Food," even if only one person filled it out.

If you want to see what they ordered, you have to open a separate sheet for "Orders" and match the names together.

MongoDB is like a box of sticky notes.

Each friend gets their own sticky note.

You can write down whatever you want on each note. If Alice has a phone number, write it down. if Bob doesn't, just leave it off.

You can list all of someone's orders directly on their sticky note, so everything you need is in one place.

In short:

SQL: Very organized, strict rules, great for things like banks where everything must fit exact rules.

MongoDB: Super flexible, easy to change, great for fast-growing apps and websites.